  "prompt": "For each country of the stores, what share of the orders came from registered customers? The share is the number of orders with a customer_id divided by the number of all orders of the stores in that country, so a big store weighs more than a small one. A store's country is its country_code, and the webshop, store_id 99, is a store in NL. Give it as a fraction between 0 and 1, rounded to 4 decimals. Return two columns, in this order: country_code and share_registered. Return one row for each country with orders. Any row order is fine.",
